{"kind":"report","text":"Approved for the Stage 2 implementation fd6f00b612d68c035cbdbc3f27ebe3c21500f079 / c96e88fc3ce2d8b910de4c38d66c9030a0a8b8c7 at exact 39430e23dcbae8e40df551dc53855a669250a79d. Primary 086ae11b7aafe7d96c5304bf5e9b256fa67405a5 is first; all 47 delivered artifacts were individually inspected for effectiveness and direct builder provenance, and I independently recomputed every exact blob/byte/SHA identity: 2,074,484 bytes, no mismatch. Normal preparation binds this review to the original Stage 2 request. This is a new verdict at the repaired head; the withdrawn 25bede37 approval at 4ec48aa1 remains withdrawn.\n\nThe two P1 causes in a7688a71 are repaired. Core 1292–1318 compares the kept evaluation's policy identity on the initial hit, competing-result hit and final read, records it on every write, and replaces mismatched rows after the existing seal fence succeeds. An unversioned preexisting row cannot match and is reevaluated. Policy identity stays cache bookkeeping, without adding it to RuleInput or changing retained inputs. Old-row compatibility is supported by source review; no separate injected-row runtime witness was run.\n\nCore 1401–1415 and 1455–1461 rereads the generation's current obligation/checker and the active policy in the sealing transaction. An invalidated pass ends completely before retention or sealing, including the no-runner path; it does not loop indefinitely over an obsolete specification. The earlier actor/revocation fact fence remains. Historical check-carried verification continues to use its named policy, and conservative activation restart leaves valid old judgments verifiable. Activation invalidates the prepared attempt/integration; recomputation schedules new work and the engine prepares under the new version. Source review also checked admission-queue recomputation and job current-owner/configuration and pre-dispatch guards. These support retirement of obsolete dispatch, not the absence of every transient stale owed row.\n\nFresh independent execution is deliberately focused: both the cache and removed-obligation carry witnesses pass under the shipped v2 declarations (2 passed, 105 unselected), and the overtaking-activation witness passes under shipped v1 (1 passed, 62 unselected). The v2 carry witness confirms recomputation before releasing its held evaluation, no extra judgment, and publication/verification of the honest log. The cache witness holds the operation/input digest equal across pass-to-block policy activation, requires two evaluations and failure before reservation. The activation witness confirms new-policy carry and continued progress. Real workerd/SQLite and real policy evaluator, with the shipped artifact/publisher/checker-service doubles; no provider proof. I checked all 22 evidence hashes, all 10 fixture identities against exact Git, loaded assertions and both successful command exits. Portable evidence is ca9d066882373c04cd1fd6728486469983a30e77; manifest SHA256 f1a0feb4a559bc321e534ce9879aa0c61f573c936cd6df929321126ef719e623. Tracked source/tests/configurations were unchanged; existing dependencies were reused.\n\nThe earlier Stage 2 requirement-by-requirement review remains usable only where source and meaning are unchanged. The former cache assumption is corrected by this review, rather than carried forward. Against 0138 the six scoped changed paths are the report, core.ts, acts.test.ts, declared-run.test.ts, carry-accounting note and invariants; all earlier 46 scoped paths remain, with declared-run added. The only product-source repair is core.ts. Initial v2 admission, explicit bindings, grants, legacy/platform handling, prepared facts and existing credential rules retain their earlier assessed behavior. Existing land/carry fact-fence source is unchanged from the independently reproduced and controlled 26872 boundary. Builder's exact-head gate report of 2,030 passing tests and reported mutation controls is recorded evidence; I did not rerun that broad gate or claim fresh control credit.\n\nP3 advisory wording corrections: core.ts 1403–1406 should distinguish policy-triggered conservative restart from obligation ineligibility that would produce decision-extra; not every activation makes a historical named-policy judgment invalid. Carry-accounting line 157 should name the recorded admission role plus current teams, rather than imply both are reread currently. The note's older claim that the land-revocation witness publishes/verifies a log also exceeds that witness's actual assertions. These are documentation qualifications, not additional runtime findings.\n\nArchitecture: policy-version ownership belongs beside the cached result, and eligibility must be checked in the transaction that commits a judgment. Existing immutable historical identities and restart machinery remain coherent. Security: stale passing policy answers no longer authorize landing under another policy; removed obligations cannot produce misleading evidence. Actor/delegation/binding and job dispatch checks remain in force. Simplification: one policy-matching helper and one conservative pass exit cover the repaired boundaries without a cache schema migration, new RuleInput field or duplicate judgment system.\n\nThis verdict closes Stage 2's requested implementation review only. Complete Stage 3 evaluation accounting and its whole-log legacy negative witness remain owed under 1e8fee4b; the proposed carry-pass contract is not adopted or built through this verdict. The inherited Stage 5 client/CLI edits are outside this Stage 2 approval, and Stage 5's remaining findings, live UI entry scope and MCP runtime/contract review remain separate. The assembled branch is not thereby approved to land as a whole. Full functionality, ownership, required final composition/gates and deliberate exact-head review remain; no schedule-based reduction or extra Jam gate is introduced.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:086ae11b7aafe7d96c5304bf5e9b256fa67405a5","binding":"assigned","head":"39430e23dcbae8e40df551dc53855a669250a79d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:53df705fae51600b34ae33e0036a273de7542999\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ca9d066882373c04cd1fd6728486469983a30e77\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c96e88fc3ce2d8b910de4c38d66c9030a0a8b8c7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ca9d066882373c04cd1fd6728486469983a30e77","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}